// COFF - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// COFF: the Common Object File Format, twenty bytes of file
// header and forty of section header before any data.
//
// Machine i386, one section, no optional header -- that last one is
// what makes this an object rather than an image. The greeting
// `Hello World!` is the section's raw data, and SizeOfRawData and
// PointerToRawData are both thirteen and sixty for it.
//
// coff: 72 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 4C 01 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |L...............|   <- 0000
// 00 00 02 01 2E 74 65 78 74 00 00 00 0C 00 00 00 |.....text.......|   <- 0010
// 00 00 00 00 0C 00 00 00 3C 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |........<.......|   <- 0020
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 20 00 50 60 48 65 6C 6C |........ .P`Hell|   <- 0030
// 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21                         |o World!|   <- 0040
